# Rules for scripts/check-risk. This header owns the evidence rules; other files point here.
# Project layer: the patterns follow this project's planned layout (architecture.md, Targets and
# Package) and approximate the platform pack's lists (platform.md: new platform capabilities and
# security-pass triggers own those lists). Revise at the skeleton ADR and at ADR-0002.
#
# Evidence counts only when the same change set adds it:
#   t2        a new ADR file in docs/decisions/, or an added line in a work/*/plan.md that starts
#             (after an optional "- ") with "T1 because"
#   security  an added line in a work/*/plan.md that starts (after an optional "- ") with
#             "Security pass:"
# A path rule also applies to a deleted file. A *-text rule is a regular expression matched
# against the lines the change set adds.
#
#   project   a file that means an Xcode project or package exists; scripts/check then fails until
#             build and tests are wired in
#
# category       pattern
project          *.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj
project          **/*.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj
project          Package.swift
project          **/Package.swift
project          project.yml
project          **/project.yml
project          Project.swift
project          **/Project.swift
t2               **/*.entitlements
t2               **/Package.swift
t2               **/project.yml
t2               **/*.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj
t2               **/Migrations/**
t2               **/*Schema*.swift
t2-text          @Model\b|registerMigration|VersionedSchema|SchemaMigrationPlan
t2-text          \bimport (GRDB|StoreKit|AuthenticationServices|Firebase|Supabase|Alamofire|RevenueCat)\b|\bURLSession\b
security         **/*.entitlements
security         **/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy
security-text    \b(SecItem\w*|kSecClass|requestAuthorization|AuthorizationCenter)\b
security-text    NSAppTransportSecurity|NS\w*UsageDescription|UIBackgroundModes
